+## New operation-state architecture
+
+### Backend
+
+New file:
+
+- `next/src-tauri/src/operation_state.rs`
+
+The desktop implementation reads Git's actual worktree-specific state directory and exposes:
+
+- active operation: `merge`, `rebase`, `cherryPick`, `revert`;
+- unresolved conflict count;
+- Continue availability;
+- Skip availability only where Git supports it;
+- Abort availability;
+- current commit and subject when Git exposes them;
+- rebase step / total where the rebase state files expose progress;
+- a human-readable operation-state message.
+
+The Tauri API adds:
+
+- `repository_operation_state(path)`
+- `control_repository_operation(path, action)`
+
+Operation controls map to Git's sequencer commands:
+
+- merge: `git merge --continue|--abort`
+- rebase: `git rebase --continue|--skip|--abort`
+- cherry-pick: `git cherry-pick --continue|--skip|--abort`
+- revert: `git revert --continue|--skip|--abort`
+
+Desktop operation commands set a non-interactive Git editor to prevent the Tauri process from hanging on an external terminal editor while accepting Git's existing operation message.
+
+Android uses `git2::RepositoryState` for detection. Controls remain explicitly disabled there until the native sequencer continuation logic is implemented.
+
+### Error model
+
+`AppError::Unsupported` is added. The current repository already referenced this variant in Android backend code even though it was missing from `error.rs`, so this also fixes an existing Android compile-path defect.
+
+### Frontend types / API
+
+New frontend data types:
+
+- `RepositoryOperationKind`
+- `RepositoryOperationAction`
+- `RepositoryOperationState`
+
+`api.ts` adds `operationState()` and `controlOperation()`.
+
+## New persistent operation UX
+
+New component:
+
+- `next/src/components/OperationBanner.tsx`
+
+The banner lives between the repository command bar and the active workspace. It remains visible regardless of whether the user is looking at Changes, History, Branches or an advanced tool.
+
+It shows:
+
+- operation name;
+- rebase progress where available;
+- current commit subject where available;
+- unresolved conflict count and next action;
+- Resolve Conflicts;
+- Continue;
+- Skip Commit where supported;
+- Abort with a destructive-action confirmation.
+
+Abort is deliberately not one-click. The confirmation is keyboard operable, supports Escape, traps Tab inside the modal, and attempts to restore focus to the trigger when the operation remains mounted.
+
+## Safety interlocks
+
+While an operation is in progress:
+
+- Pull is disabled.
+- Push is disabled.
+- Branch create / checkout is disabled.
+- Normal Commit is disabled.
+- Worktree create/prune is disabled.
+- Submodule update/sync is disabled.
+- Stash push/pop is disabled.
+- Maintenance and mutating LFS actions are disabled.
+- Read-only inspection such as Fetch, worktree listing, stash listing, reflog, fsck and LFS lock listing remains available.
+
+The Changes view remains writable for Stage / Unstage because staging is the normal mechanism for marking conflict resolutions.
+
+## Additional UX correctness fix
+
+The previous Submodules screen used `submodule_sync` as its automatic refresh operation. Sync changes local submodule URL configuration, so opening a view could silently perform a write. Automatic refresh now performs no submodule write; the screen explains the structured-status backend gap and Sync remains an explicit user action.
+
+## Existing v2 improvements retained
+
+- repository-state-first navigation;
+- resizable/collapsible panes;
+- separate Conflicts / Staged / Unstaged groups;
+- independent partially-staged selections;
+- structured worktree list;
+- proper Clone dialog;
+- searchable keyboard command palette;
+- branch manager and remote/local separation UI;
+- compact engineering-oriented desktop density.
+
+## Optional backend correctness patch retained
+
+`docs/backend-correctness.patch` still fixes two pre-existing CLI backend defects:
+
+1. local branches containing `/` are no longer misclassified as remotes;
+2. `git status --porcelain=v1 -z` rename/copy source paths are consumed correctly instead of appearing as fake file rows.
+
+## Validation performed
+
+Frontend:
+
+- 14 TypeScript / TSX files parsed with TypeScript 5.8.3;
+- an additional semantic TypeScript pass was run with local React/Tauri API shims so cross-file prop/API contracts were checked without downloading npm dependencies;
+- CSS braces balanced after final edits.
+
+Backend logic:
+
+Real temporary Git repositories were created and exercised with Git 2.47.3:
+
+- merge conflict detected, staged resolution, `merge --continue` succeeded;
+- rebase conflict detected, `rebase --skip` succeeded;
+- cherry-pick conflict detected, `cherry-pick --abort` restored state;
+- revert conflict detected, `revert --abort` restored state.
+
+This validated the on-disk state markers and command semantics used by the Rust operation-state controller.
+
+Rust compilation itself could not be run in this container because `cargo`, `rustc` and `rustfmt` are not installed. Rust source received structural brace checks, but the definitive Rust validation remains `cargo check` / `npm run tauri dev` on the development machine.
+
